                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "*WARNING: This game has been reviewed from a FPS veteran perspective. Newcomer discretion is advised.*\n\nAs far as I wanted to enjoy HARP Vefa, a historical FPS made by Turkish devs, I simply cannot recommend it due to some frustrating game design and technical issues...\n\nPOSITIVES\n+ Hilarious and cheesy fight scene\n+ Decent visuals\n+ Lighting effects\n+ Draw distance\n+ The map scale\n\nNEGATIVES\n- Enemy AI shoots at you with pinpoint accuracy\n- Enemy AI simply camp in their spot\n- Environment does not provide cover\n- Hit detection issues\n- No save feature\n- Poor optimization\n- Very linear level design\n- No keybinding menu\n- Low polycount models\n\nI'm warning you. The game is really difficult, but not in a good way. The beginning consist of walking through an alley of snipers and dying every minute...\n\nRequesting a REFUND!\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PgerstUyvos\n\nRating:\n3.5 / 10",
